{"qid":"Q224","names":["Republic of Croatia"],"title":"Republic of Croatia","endonym":{"native":"Hrvatska","lang":"hr"},"capsule":"The Republic of Croatia (Republika Hrvatska) declared independence from Yugoslavia on 25 June 1991, with that independence recognized internationally on 15 January 1992, inaugurating the entry recorded here. The country fought the Croatian War of Independence (1991–1995) against Yugoslav federal forces and Serbian paramilitaries; the Croat-majority areas held by Serb forces (Republic of Serbian Krajina) were reintegrated by Operation Storm in August 1995. Croatia joined NATO in April 2009 and the European Union on 1 July 2013, and adopted the euro on 1 January 2023, completing its integration into Euro-Atlantic institutions under the presidency of Zoran Milanović and successive prime ministers.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The territorial extent of Croatia post-1995 is fully documented from UN and EU administrative records; the boundaries are internationally recognized except for a minor ongoing dispute with Slovenia over the Bay of Piran.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Croatia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croatia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Croatian War of Independence","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croatian_War_of_Independence"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Operation Storm","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Storm"}],"britannica":"place/Croatia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Croatia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q982371","name":"Franjo Gregurić","start":1991,"end":1992,"image":"Cvjetni trg simul 20160601 DSC 5221 (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://com